IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `taa-types`
IMPORT `taa-dates`

-- Tax Administration Act 1994 — GOAL 1: EMPLOYMENT INCOME INFORMATION AND
-- TAX CODES.
--
--   "Which group is the employer in, by when must it deliver employment
--    income information for a payday, and does the employee have a
--    non-notified tax code?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1994_166.txt — ss 23D-23H,
-- 23M, 24E.

§ `Goal 1 — employment income information and tax codes`

-- s 23F "(1) An employer is included in the non-electronic group if the
-- employer— (a) meets either of the requirements set out in subsection (5)
-- or has an exemption under section 23G; and (b) does not deliver ...
-- electronically ...; and (c) is not included in the new group. ... (5) ...
-- (a) an employer other than [a new employer] must have gross amounts of tax
-- payable for the preceding tax year that are below the threshold amount: (b)
-- a new employer must have total accumulated amounts of tax that are below
-- the threshold amount. (6) The threshold amount ... is— (a) $50,000". s 23H
-- "(1) An employer is included in the new group if the employer becomes an
-- employer in a tax year. (2) The new-employer period is the 6-month
-- period". s 23H(5): one who delivers electronically joins the online group.
-- s 23E(1): otherwise the online group.
@ref ss 23D, 23E(1), 23F(1), (5)-(6), 23H(1)-(2), (5)
@export The group an employer belongs to for delivering employment income information under ss 23D-23H of the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ): the new group for a new employer's first 6 months unless it delivers electronically; the non-electronic group if it does not deliver electronically and its PAYE and ESCT are below $50,000 (or it has an exemption); otherwise the online group. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN Employer  @desc Whether it delivers electronically, its PAYE and ESCT, whether it is new and when it started, and any exemption
      payday IS A DATE  @desc The payday in question
GIVETH AN `Employer group`
`the employer group of` e `on` payday MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF e's `delivers employment income information electronically` THEN `the online group`
        IF     e's `a new employer`
           AND (CONSIDER e's `started employing on`
                WHEN JUST s THEN payday LESS THAN `add months` s 6
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
           AND e's `PAYE and ESCT for the preceding tax year` LESS THAN 50000
            THEN `the new group, delivering non-electronically`
        IF e's `PAYE and ESCT for the preceding tax year` LESS THAN 50000 OR e's `has a s 23G exemption`
            THEN `the non-electronic group`
        OTHERWISE `the online group`

-- s 23E(2) "An employer in the online group must deliver their employment
-- income information for a payday— ... (b) within 2 working days after
-- payday." s 23F "(2) An employer in the non-electronic group must deliver
-- ... (b) within 10 working days after payday. (3) ... may choose to treat the
-- payday as— (a) the day on which the employer makes a PAYE income payment
-- ...; or (b) ... (i) for an amount paid ... [from] the 1st day of a month
-- [to] the 15th ..., the 15th of the month; and (ii) ... [from] the 16th ...
-- [to] the last day of the month, the last day of the month." s 23H(3)-(4):
-- the new group likewise, 10 working days, with the same choice.
@ref ss 23E(2), 23F(2)-(3), 23H(3)-(4)
@export The last day an employer may deliver employment income information for a payday under ss 23E-23H of the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ): 2 working days after payday for the online group; 10 working days after payday for the non-electronic and new groups, which may treat paydays as the 15th or the last day of the month. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN Employer  @desc The employer's facts, including the twice-monthly payday choice
      payday IS A DATE  @desc The day of the PAYE income payment
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE  @desc The Matariki Observance Days
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to deliver employment income information, employer` e `, payday` payday `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    CONSIDER `the employer group of` e `on` payday
    WHEN `the online group` THEN `the` 2 `th working day after` payday `, Matariki days` matariki
    OTHERWISE `the` 10 `th working day after` treated `, Matariki days` matariki
    WHERE
        treated MEANS
            IF   NOT e's `chooses the twice-monthly payday`
            THEN payday
            ELSE IF   DATE_DAY payday AT MOST 15
                 THEN Date 15 (DATE_MONTH payday) (DATE_YEAR payday)
                 ELSE Date (`Days in month` payday) (DATE_MONTH payday) (DATE_YEAR payday)

-- s 23M "An employer who stops employing employees, intending that the
-- cessation is permanent, must notify the Commissioner that employment has
-- ended within 30 working days after the date on which they stop employing
-- employees."
@ref s 23M
GIVEN stopped IS A DATE, matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify that employment has ended, stopped on` stopped `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    `the` 30 `th working day after` stopped `, Matariki days` matariki

-- s 24E "(1) An employee, other than a person referred to in section 24D, has
-- a non-notified tax code if— (a) the employee has not notified their
-- employer of— (i) their name; and (ii) their tax file number; and (iii) their
-- tax code; and (b) the Commissioner has not provided the employer with a tax
-- code ...; and (c) the employee is not a non-resident seasonal worker". Read
-- as: not having notified all three (fork F1). The rate is 0.45 (Income Tax
-- Act 2007, schedule 2, part A, cl 3).
@ref s 24E(1); Income Tax Act 2007 schedule 2 part A cl 3
@export Whether an employee has a non-notified tax code under s 24E of the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ) — PAYE then at 45 cents in the dollar: if they have not notified their employer of all of their full name, tax file number and tax code, the Commissioner has not provided a code, and they are not a non-resident seasonal worker or a person under s 24D. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS AN Employee  @desc What the employee has notified, any code from the Commissioner, and whether they are a seasonal worker or under s 24D
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a non-notified tax code` p IF
        NOT p's `a person referred to in s 24D`
    AND NOT (p's `notified their full name` AND p's `notified their tax file number` AND p's `notified their tax code`)
    AND NOT p's `the Commissioner has provided a tax code`
    AND NOT p's `a non-resident seasonal worker`
